---------------------------------------------------------------------\nKidney & Joint Cat Food KJ2 – For Chronic Kidney Disease (https://uk.virbac.com/products/kidney-joint-cat-food-kj2-for-chronic-kidney-disease)\nciteturn66search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: text/html; For intermediate kidney disease: KJ2 Kidney & Joint , a low-phosphorus cat food. Protects kidneys, promotes joint mobility, manages denutrition.\nVETERINARY HPM® KJ2 Kidney & Joint contains high fat and energy density to avoid denutrition, along with moderate, high-quality proteins (35%) for cats with mid-stage kidney disease. This limited protein level and choice of quality proteins restrict the production of uraemic toxins while preserving your cat’s muscle mass. It also promotes healthy weight maintenance, supporting physical activity and reducing the burden on the joints.\nLow in phosphorous to support kidney function\nAs kidney disease progresses, the kidneys become less efficient at filtering out phosphorus. This can further damage the kidneys and other tissues. VETERINARY HPM® KJ2 Kidney & Joint contains limited protein, high omega-3 fatty acids, and a low level of phosphorus (0.55%) to support your cat’s kidney function. It also includes chitosan to bind to phosphorus, further limiting phosphorus levels available in the body.\nA blend of supportive nutrients to care for the joints\nLike kidney disease, joint problems like osteoarthritis are common as cats age. VETERINARY HPM® KJ2 Kidney & Joint features a range of nutrients designed to support joint health:\n• Omega-3 fatty acids help limit inflammation that can lead to joint pain and degeneration.\n• Egg shell membrane is rich in collagen, glucosamine and other nutrients naturally found in the joints.\n• Chondroitin sulphate helps supports joint cartilage and supports lubrication.\n• Chitosan optimises the breakdown and absorption of chondroitin.\nVETERINARY HPM® KJ2 Kidney & Joint is an ideal dry cat food for kidney issues in both adult and senior cats. With the delicious, meaty taste of quality animal proteins, you can be confident your cat will love the flavour. You can also tailor it to your cat’s needs and preferences by combining it with VETERINARY HPM® KJ2 Kidney & Joint Wet mousse.\n\nVETERINARY HPM® KJ2 Kidney & Joint Dry is a cat food for cats with chronic kidney disease at IRIS stage 2, also known as intermediate or mid-stage kidney disease. It is only intended for adult and senior cats, and is suitable for cats with or without osteoarthritis, a degenerative joint disease.\nIf your cat has early-stage kidney disease (stage 1) or only has osteoarthritis, they may be better suited to VETERINARY HPM® KJ1 Early Kidney & Joint Dry. If they have advanced kidney disease (stages 3-4), VETERINARY HPM® KJ3 Advanced Kidney & Joint Dry may be more suitable.\nAlways check with your vet or vet nurse before giving your cat a clinical cat food for kidney issues to make sure it’s safe and appropriate for their individual needs.\n\nThe International Renal Interest Society, or IRIS, classification system is a way of describing how advanced a cat’s kidney dysfunction or disease is. It tells your vet how well your cat’s kidneys are functioning and helps them to plan the most appropriate treatment, including diet.\nKidney disease is grouped into one of four IRIS stages:\n• Stage 1 refers to early-stage kidney dysfunction.\n• Stage 2 refers to intermediate or mid-stage kidney disease.\n• Stage 3 refers to advanced kidney disease.\n### How does VETERINARY HPM® KJ2 Kidney & Joint Dry support my cat’s kidney health?\n\nVETERINARY HPM® KJ2 Kidney & Joint Dry is formulated to help support your cats kidney function. It does this with:\n• A moderate amount of quality proteins to preserve muscle mass.\n• Low phosphorus content to reduce strain on the kidneys.\n• Chitosan to bind phosphorous and reduce levels even further.\n\n### How does VETERINARY HPM® KJ2 Kidney & Joint Dry support my cat’s joint health?\n\nVETERINARY HPM® KJ2 Kidney & Joint Dry contains a range of nutrients designed to keep the joints mobile, flexible and healthy:\n• Omega-3 fatty acids help limit inflammation that can lead to joint pain and degeneration.\n• Egg shell membrane is rich in collagen, glucosamine and other nutrients naturally found in the joints.\n• Chondroitin sulphate helps to prevent the breakdown of joint cartilage and supports lubrication.\n• Chitosan optimises the breakdown and absorption of chondroitin.\n\n### Does this food come in a wet format?\n\nYes. If you prefer to give your cat wet food or as a combination, try VETERINARY HPM® KJ2 Kidney & Joint Wet instead. It features the same high-quality animal proteins, very low phosphorus content and joint-supportive nutrients, in a delicious mousse your cat will love.\n\n### How much VETERINARY HPM® KJ2 Kidney & Joint Dry should I feed my cat?\n\nYou can find recommended rations for VETERINARY HPM® KJ2 Kidney & Joint Dry on this page and on the packaging. Remember that the recommended rations are based on your cat’s current body weight and whether this weight is overweight, normal or underweight for them. If you are unsure what a normal weight is for your cat, consult your vet or vet nurse for advice.\n### Can VETERINARY HPM® KJ2 Kidney & Joint Dry be given as part of a mixed wet/dry diet?\n\nYes, you can feed a combination of wet and dry food. To help you determine how much food to feed of each the feeding table provided on this page can be used as a guide.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUrinary problems (https://www.advance-affinity.com/cs/cat/specific-needs/urinary-problems)\nciteturn66search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; The ADVANCE URINARY solution is a diet that helps to reduce the risk of the formation of common crystals, thanks to urinary dilution and crystallisation ... Read more\n## Discover the\nADVANCE VETERINARY\nDIETS URINARY